{"c":[{"id":"dbb04edae3a352a3","sum":"H7: judge a18_vm_walk.py results.json with vm_results.py; TextEdit fix ⌘Z is one pid-directed ⌘Z; alternatives never withdraw for room. D2-06/V1b: goal steps only via goalAccept, presses hand off, GoalRuns.blocked null after a segment; unreadable clipboard items refuse paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"238a84aaa66db02b","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after each check (judge with vm_results.py); TextEdit writing-fix ⌘Z is one pid-directed ⌘Z, others AX restore; alternatives never withdraw for room (inline or capsule); undrawn offers withdraw; late draws publish(shown:false)+reveal.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1cb02aaa5824eced","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check (judge with vm_results.py, test with test_a18_vm_walk.py); a writing fix's Cmd-Z in TextEdit is one pid-directed Cmd-Z (nativeUndo) with no AX restore after; other apps keep the AX restore.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T102528Z-49569322ff77aac5","text":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check and in finally; VM jobs judge it with scripts/vm_results.py, never the transcript's last line. test_a18_vm_walk.py runs the walk against stand-ins on any Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T102528Z-b2fd96251e54b1a0","text":"H7: a writing fix's ⌘Z in TextEdit sends TextEdit one pid-directed ⌘Z (UndoGrant.strategy nativeUndo, NativeUndoApps); nothing restores text after it is sent. Other apps keep the AX restore, which TextEdit-like apps record as a new undo step.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"95ce68e7dc925e47","sum":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py results.json is judged by vm_results.py; alternatives never withdraw for room (fitsInField picks inline or capsule, capsules below the caret line else above); undrawn offers withdraw; drawn-after-publish uses publish(shown: false) + reveal.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T102543Z-0a3850ef6a0fa08f","text":"H7: a18_vm_walk.py writes results.json after every check and in finally; VM jobs judge it with scripts/vm_results.py, not the transcript tail. test_a18_vm_walk.py runs the walk against stand-ins on any Mac.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T102543Z-4af89305464255b2","text":"H7: alternatives never withdraw for want of inline room: fitsInField picks inline or capsule; CaretLinePlacement puts capsules below the caret line, else above. Undrawn offers withdraw (notDrawn); offers drawn after publish use publish(shown: false) + reveal.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"180a63d9d112870b","sum":"D2-06/V1b: 'Continue' never classified; goal press only e:reveal on 'Next'; page presses hand off; only goalAccept runs goal steps, no taskControl resume; GoalRuns.blocked must go null after a segment or undo fails. Unreadable clipboard items refuse the paste.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cf5de0df55b6d70e","sum":"D2-06: 'Continue' is unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive dialogs); the one goal press is e:reveal on a whole 'Next'; page presses hand off. Only goalAccept runs a goal's steps; taskControl never resumes one; targets are Target.exact, no fallback.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1712f90f65a11b14","text":"D2-06: 'Continue' is deliberately unclassified at every press boundary (it confirms destructive macOS dialogs); the one goal press capability is e:reveal on a whole 'Next' (goals/capabilities.ts). Page presses are always hand-offs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T105430Z-1ba2dff3c7f2e7e3","text":"D2-06: only a goalAccept (goalId, segment, digest) runs a goal's steps; a goal task (GoalRuns.owns) is never resumed by taskControl, and a pause stops it. Goal targets are Target.exact (key+role, a button's label): resolveLocally never falls back for them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2fca48002a55d2e6","sum":"D2-06/V1b: GoalRuns.blocked (inside authorize before every act) must return null once a segment ends, or goal undo is refused. A clipboard item with no readable type (a lone public.file-url) refuses the paste; lastInsertion.clipboardTypes shows what was saved.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T105431Z-2d9978b4db29946e","text":"D2-06: GoalRuns.blocked runs inside Helper.authorize before every act; it must return null once a segment ends, or a goal task's undo (undoBlocked -> authorize) is refused.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T110217Z-f50d1fce02c90ec1","text":"V1b: Caret pasted over a clipboard whose 2nd item held only public.file-url and the restore dropped it, reporting restored. Items with no readable type now refuse the paste; lastInsertion.clipboardTypes shows what Caret's save read.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c11a295989bc0680","sum":"B30-H7b: plan Asks become goals for goal hosts; name regexes stay case-sensitive; drafts are whole facts. Router errors (R2) are the host's missed budget; pid-posted keys skip the tap; RouteFollower binds by text digest; only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"73770d76091cc26a","sum":"B30: plan-route Asks become goals for goal hosts (planAsk goals:true); keep name regexes case-sensitive (i folds \\p{Lu}). Goal writes skip Cc/Bcc/Subject, To = answered From. Drafts checked as whole typed facts; close holes with whole-expression rules.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"eaeefb243874759f","sum":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan becomes a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true -> AskGoal, helper.offerGoal); others keep planTask/planWithCode. A JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to lower case: keep name patterns case-sensitive.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-9e86109ce30422ae","text":"B30: a goal-planning host's Ask with route plan is offered as a D2-06 goal (planAsk goals:true returns AskGoal; helper.offerGoal); other consumers keep planTask/planWithCode. planAsk overloads: goals absent/false types as AskDraft.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120548Z-b6135cb945f89335","text":"B30: JS regex with the i flag folds \\p{Lu} to match lower case too; a case-insensitive name pattern let 'Thanks, I'll pay' skip Jev. Keep name patterns case-sensitive.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d827b4876610494b","sum":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc/Subject; To takes only the From of the answered message (drafts.ts senderOf, rechecked at accept). Drafted text is checked as whole typed facts, every digit in a fact; fix holes with whole-expression rules, never token allowlists.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T120548Z-c27c662d572bf540","text":"B30: goal writes never touch Cc/Bcc or Subject, and To takes only the From address in the header block of the message the reply window answers (Re: <subject>), rechecked at accept (drafts.ts senderOf). D2-06 scenes rely on mailWindow line 0 being its From header.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T120623Z-4f068d6de508aa09","text":"B30: drafted goal text is checked in goals/drafts.ts as whole typed facts; every digit must land in a fact, and a from value ref stands for its source window or memory. Two reviews found recombination holes: add whole-expression rules, never token allowlists.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ee5e6005a3f942f5","sum":"H6-H7b: pid-posted keys skip the tap (route through debug 'key char:x' to stamp latency); a router error is outcome error (R2), a missed budget for the host; bindings from sha256(text+NUL+'unknown') digests; only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots the clipboard.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"54a198c67235f383","sum":"H6: pid-posted keys skip the host tap (no latency stamp); ghost_latency_routing.py routes each key through debug 'key char:x' first. Since R2/H8 a failed router call is outcome error + failure, and RouteFollower treats it as that context's missed budget.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T132640Z-116806e783493150","text":"H6: keys posted with CGEventPostToPid never pass the host's event tap, so its latency recorder gets no key stamp; ghost_latency_routing.py routes each key through the debug hook 'key char:x' first, which stamps it, then posts it to the fixture.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T132640Z-ec39615ba3d313e7","text":"H6: the helper publishes a failed or low-confidence router call as a plain abstain (no reason on the wire), so the host cannot fall back on a router error; only a decision that never arrives triggers RouteFollower's budget fallback.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"40260a53530a61ef","sum":"H6: RouteFollower binds the reader's window id/key from a decision whose textRevision is sha256(text+NUL+'unknown')[:16]; empty fields stay tentative. H7b: only ReconcilingClipboard.check snapshots; every posted key asks mayPost; restored = byte-for-byte re-read.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T132833Z-3831e1a92c996341","text":"H6: the host can't compute the reader's window id/key; RouteFollower binds them from a routeDecision whose textRevision is sha256(text+NUL+'unknown')[:16]. Empty fields share that digest, so their binding stays tentative until the host's revision is echoed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T133211Z-54e0f06319860375","text":"H7b: only ReconcilingClipboard.check makes a ClipboardSnapshot; the executor arms it before KeyType's inserter, every posted key asks mayPost, and restored means a fresh read at the restore's own count matched type for type, byte for byte.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
